Subject: [PATCH] feat(phase 15.6.5): add Sales Return Core with double-entry
 ledger

- database/migrations/014_sales_return.sql: SalesReturnInvoices,
  SalesReturnInvoiceItems, SalesReturnInvoiceItemLayers (additive,
  IF OBJECT_ID(...) IS NULL guarded). Account 4100 (already seeded in
  009_accounting_core.sql) is referenced, not recreated.
- services/sales_service.py (append-only, create_sales_invoice untouched):
  ACCOUNT_SALES_RETURN, _build_sales_return_journal_lines,
  _get_sales_invoice_item_returnable, create_sales_return_invoice,
  get_sales_return_invoices, get_sales_return_invoice_items,
  get_sales_invoice_returnable_items.
  * Multi-layer FIFO restoration tracked per original
    SalesInvoiceItemLayers consumption record via
    SalesReturnInvoiceItemLayers, supporting partial/multi-stage returns
    without mutating the original SalesInvoiceItemLayers rows.
  * Serial/IMEI return: Sold -> InStock, SoldInInvoiceItemRef preserved,
    no SalesReturnInvoiceItemLayers rows created for serial items.
  * Stock += qty, Cardex MovementType='SellReturn'.
  * Journal: 4100 Dr net, 2200 Dr tax (if>0), 1100 Cr net+tax,
    1200 Dr cost, 5000 Cr cost. Account 4000 never used. Posted on the
    same cursor/transaction as the return invoice (atomic with rollback).
  * Audit entry written only after successful commit.
  * Unit price always read from the original SalesInvoiceItems row, never
    trusted from caller input.
- tests/test_sales_return_service.py: 39 new tests (validation, single/
  multi-layer FIFO incl. the exact multi-stage partial-return scenario
  from the brief, serial ownership/status/duplicate/already-returned,
  stock/cardex, balanced journal + account mapping + no-4000 + conditional
  2200, rollback on over-return and on missing/inactive ledger accounts,
  commit-before-audit ordering, pure _build_sales_return_journal_lines
  tests). Full regression: 168 previously passing + 39 new = 207 passed.

SQL SERVER INTEGRATION: NOT VERIFIED (no real SQL Server connection
available in this sandbox; verified against a fake cursor/connection
that mirrors the exact SQL this code issues, same pattern as
test_sales_service.py / test_inventory_service.py).
